findings.body:
The `EmbeddingServerAppInsideIframe_WithCompressionEnabled_Fails` assertion joins the two regexes with `&&`, but its own failure message says the log should match *one of* the CSP patterns. The old pattern needs the literal `Refused to frame` and the new one needs `Framing`, so no single browser log entry can satisfy both. The test will fail whatever wording Chrome emits, and this affects every `NoneAncestor*` blocked-compression test class.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="107-110"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The intent is "either wording passes". That requires `||`, not `&&`.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="107-110"}
Assert.True(
    ParseErrorMessageRegexOld.IsMatch(logs[0].Message) ||
    ParseErrorMessageRegexNew.IsMatch(logs[0].Message),
    $"Expected log message to match one of the CSP error patterns: {ParseErrorMessageRegexOld} or {ParseErrorMessageRegexNew}. Actual: {logs[0].Message}");

The internal source-build job moves its pool image from `1es-mariner-2` to `1es-azurelinux-3`. Nothing else in this repo uses that image name, so the change can't be checked from the diff. If the image isn't present in the `NetCore1ESPool-Internal` / `NetCore1ESPool-Svc-Internal` pools, the release/9.0 internal source-build job will queue indefinitely or fail.

::diff{file="eng/common/core-templates/job/source-build.yml" lines="65-70"}

This is an arcade-inherited infra change. Confirm the image is available to these pools, ideally with a pipeline run on the release branch, before merging. If it isn't yet available, the pin should stay on the previous image.
